Description: Implements sample size planning for a future study from the summary
    statistics of a prior study, correcting the prior effect for publication bias
    and uncertainty so the planned study attains its target statistical power more
    reliably than methods that take a sample effect size at face value. Covers the
    independent and dependent 't' test, between-subjects, within-subjects, and
    split-plot factorial analysis of variance, and multiple regression. The method
    is described in Anderson, Kelley, and Maxwell (2017) <doi:10.1177/0956797617723724>.
    The noncentrality parameter underlying the correction is obtained by direct
    numerical root finding, a more accurate approach than a fixed grid search that
    also removes an internal upper limit on the parameter. A small number of
    planned sample sizes therefore differ slightly from versions 1.x; the new
    values are more accurate.
